Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||01-21-2001||07:18 PM||||In '97 I bought a red 88 GT with tan beechwood interior. The factory leather seats were and still are not in the best of shape... And with the 2001 San Francisco Fiero Fest coming up soon in July, I'd like to have them restored.<P>I know Mr. Mike's has a leather seat replacement. I just wanted some advice as to options that I have in restoring the seats. I've seen pics on the Mr. Mikes website and the seats look great. How close are they to the factory leather seats?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/SouthBeach/Cove/2449/finalfront.jpg">  1987 SE - 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-21-2001||10:48 PM||||I also have an 88 GT with the leather seats.  In my car the seats were in good shape.  Mr Mikes seats are really very very nice, but do not look like the stock Fiero seats. At least most of the seats I've seen do not look like the stock ones. Go to his web site <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mrmikes.com</A>   He does produce a nice product.||||reg||1
